Download the current PR description from GitHub using `gh pr view 1 --json body --jq '.body'` and save it to `/workspace/.pr_temp/current_pr_description.md` (creating the directory if it doesn't exist).

Read the full content of that file, then create an updated version at `/workspace/.pr_temp/updated_pr_description.md` that reflects the current state of the project. Consider:

- Update the version number (check `PLUGIN_VERSION` in `beat_saber_deluxe/src/main.cpp`)
- Update the song list if any songs changed (check `deploy_all.sh` for current targets)
- Add any new bug fixes or features since the PR was last updated
- Update CI/CD status (check if CI passes, what artifacts are produced)
- Keep the same structure and tone as the original

Then run a diff between old and new:
```bash
diff -u /workspace/.pr_temp/current_pr_description.md /workspace/.pr_temp/updated_pr_description.md > /workspace/.pr_temp/pr_description_diff.md
```

Present the 3 file paths to the user and ask them to review. Once they type "approved", push the update with:
```bash
gh api repos/free5ty1e/BeatSaberPcCustomSongToPs4InstallConverter/pulls/1 --method PATCH --field body="$(cat /workspace/.pr_temp/updated_pr_description.md | python3 -c 'import sys,json; print(json.dumps(sys.stdin.read()))')"
```

(Use the REST API directly — `gh pr edit` has a known GraphQL deprecation issue that causes it to fail on this repo.)
